[E0314] Error: `str` cannot be read by a C function that takes more
    ╭─[ err/129_variadic_calls/main.wip:23:20 ]
    │
 23 │     printf("%s\n", text)
    │                    ──┬─  
    │                      ╰─── not a value C reads there
    │ 
    │ Help: a `str` has no NUL: give C a `cstring`, or the two of `text.len()` and the bytes
    │ 
    │ Note: what follows the declared parameters is read one at a time, so it is the scalars C knows: integers of up to 64 bits, the floats, `bool`, `cstring` and `ptr<T>`
────╯
